<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hessian Ludwig Railway</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1845–1897</span> · Also known as Hessische Ludwigsbahn</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hessian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ludwig-railway">Ludwig Railway</a> was a private railway company of the Grand Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a>, named after Grand Duke Louis III. Founded in 1845 and based in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mainz">Mainz</a>, it built lines linking Mainz with Worms, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darmstadt">Darmstadt</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankfurt">Frankfurt</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhineland">Rhineland</a>. It was taken over in 1897 by the joint Prussian and Hessian state railways.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hessian-ludwig-railway.jpg" alt="Hessian Ludwig Railway" width="320" height="209" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ludwigsbahnhof_Darmstadt.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
